+`.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines. Inside double quotes, `\"` and `\\` are unescaped; single-quoted values are taken literally. An unquoted value ends at a ` #` (space then hash), so `KEY=15 # seconds` gives `15`. Lines that are not `KEY=value` are ignored.
+
+## Checking the configuration
+
+Run `python -m payhook check` to list required settings that are missing.
+
+Run `python -m payhook doctor` to print every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), along with the path of the `.env` file that was read. Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are printed only as a character count, so the output can be pasted into a support ticket.
 
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
